2015-03-06 12:04 GMT+03:00 guskant <gusni.kantu@gmail.com>:

> Why don't you make any comment on {de'iV} series? Only five more words are
> enough for preventing cultural difficulties on expressions of date.
>

Maybe they are fine, idk. The community needs to use them.

But I think splicing month is still related to {masti} so {mai'o+masti}
might be better.

Also I assume you agreed that {mai'o}  can sometimes be the only option.
I just want something simple but universal.

Here are the test sentences:
Splicing in time.
*de'i li pa [pi'e pa] - on [January] 1
*ba de'i li pa ki ti = tomorrow
*de'i li pa poi se masti ki ti = next month
*ti'u li re pi'e xo'e = at 2 o'clock
*ti'u li re = at 2:00
*ba ti'u li pa ki ti /  ca lo remoi be lo cacra? = next hour
*ti'u li pa poi se snidu ki ti = next second
*ca lo pamoi be lo cacra be li re = during the first two hours

No doubt, this {ki ti} should be replaced with something more precise.

Additionally,
*on the first day of the week.

